==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to produce a state where two audit entries for the same task share identical (task, op, actor, actorRole, team) tuples — exactly the fingerprint of an in-place mutation or duplicate-overwrite. The injection forces two structurally identical entries to exist, which both assertions should catch.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditImmutableAndPersists
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditImmutableAndPersists: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnlyOwnerCanChangeSharedWith  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_OnlyOwnerCanChangeSharedWith.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Mutation with opKind=PatchSharedWith whose caller is not the task owner. The injection forces exactly this situation — a non-owner mutation against shared_with — which both assertions should catch as a violation of the owner-only share-control invariant.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ShareesSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_ShareesSameTeam.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a task's sharedWith set to contain a user from a different team, violating the cross-team isolation invariant. The injection forces a sharee from a foreign team to appear in a task's share list.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_SameTeamSharing, FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation
      - FR_012_SameTeamSharing: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_MutationLinkedToAuditEntries  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_MutationLinkedToAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows a Mutation with an empty mutAuditEntries set, meaning a successful state change produced no audit record. The injection forces a mutation with no audit entries, which both audit-completeness assertions should catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_PerEventAuditEntries
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_PerEventAuditEntries: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows an audit entry whose snapshotted actorRole differs from the actor user's actual role — a misattribution. The injection forces a mismatch between the recorded role and the actor's real role.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_016_AuditEntryContents
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditEntryContents: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OutsiderDeniedAll  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_OutsiderDeniedAll.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the permission matrix to grant an Outsider access to GetTask (or any task-level operation), violating the cross-team byte-equivalent isolation contract. The injection directly inserts an Outsider → GetTask allow cell into the matrix.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_014_ByteEquivalentNotFound, LeastPrivilege
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_ByteEquivalentNotFound: PASS (vacuous?)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)

